{"content":[{"c":["ADONI-BEZEK"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Title of the Canaanite king of Bezek, a city in northern Palestine. Soon after Joshua’s death, the tribes of Judah and Simeon defeated Adoni-bezek and amputated his thumbs and big toes. Adoni-bezek himself had treated many captured kings that way, so he regarded his fate as divine retribution (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.5-7","r":"Judg.1.5-7","rawR":"Judg.1.5-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.5-7","value":"Judg.1.5-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:5-7"},"). Some have suggested that he and Adoni-zedek (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.10.1","r":"Josh.10.1","rawR":"Josh.10.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.10.1","value":"Josh.10.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 10:1"},") were the same person."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AdoniBezek","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:5-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.5-7","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.5-7","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.5-7"},{"anchorText":"Jos 10:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.10.1","rawQueryValue":"Josh.10.1","sourceRefExact":"Josh.10.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d8f9a2c75c6fde5bce144fbdcdd539adaff9544ecc9ab536b5be1a2869654093","sourceItemName":"AdoniBezek","sourceItemOrder":130,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AdoniBezek","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Adoni-Bezek","title":"Adoni-Bezek","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}